# ============================================================
# migrations/README
#
# This folder is managed by Flask-Migrate (which uses Alembic internally).
# You should NOT manually create or edit files here.
#
# HOW TO USE:
#
# 1. Run this ONCE to initialise the migrations folder:
#       flask --app run db init
#
# 2. Whenever you change a model (add/remove a column, new table, etc.):
#       flask --app run db migrate -m "describe what changed"
#    This auto-generates a new migration script in migrations/versions/
#
# 3. To apply all pending migrations to your MySQL database:
#       flask --app run db upgrade
#
# 4. To roll back the last migration:
#       flask --app run db downgrade
#
# Think of migrations as "git commits for your database schema."
# ============================================================
